> Gethsemane Jesus and his party had retired to Gethsemane, at the full moon, just outside the city walls, for supper under the cool of the ancient olive trees. It had been an eventful couple of days since his arrival. His reputation as a healer and preacher around Galilee in the years before had preceded him, and everywhere he went crowds flocked to him, some nearly hysterical and some just curious about this new troublemaker. He had certainly attracted the attention of the established priesthood, not least of the local administration, fearful of disorder in the always volatile town.
